< So, let's just start off by saying Cheese Festivals never, ever worked out in my favor...
> Nii, alustame välja ütleme Juustu Festivalid pole midagi töötanud minu teenes

< I can remember...
> Ma mäletan...

< There were two of them when I was nine-years-old and both of them ended up with me...
> Seal oli kaks nemad kui ma olin üheksa aastane ja mõlemad lõpetasid minuga.

< Well, how do they put it...
> Noh, kuidas nemad panid...

< Forever alone.
> Alatiselt üksi.

< And now...
> Ja nüüd...

< It was that time of year again.
> See oli aasta kord jälle.

< Hillwood was going to have another one.
> Hillwoodi läheb saama teise uut.

< And I wasn't looking forward to it.
> Ja ma ei ole vaadanudki.

< Because I knew it would be filled with people who were happier than me.
> Sellepärast, et ma teatsin tahan olla koos inimene kes on rõõmsad kui mina.

< They would be having a good time, laughing...enjoying their lives.
> Nemad lähevad hästi korral, naeravad... nautivad tema elud.

< Their loves...
> Nemad armastused...

< And the one thing that made me truly happy...
> Ja üks tingimus see tegi mulle tõsiselt rõõmsaks...

< Well it made me so miserable every time the Festival came to town.
> See tegi mulle kõik õnnetu iga kordselt Festivali tuli linnasse.

< I hate that.
> Ma vihkan seda.

< It really pisses me off...
> Olen täiesti pettunud mind...

< ...
> ...

< ......
> ......

< This all began on a morning pretty much exactly like any other.
> See algas kõik hommikust palju isegi nagu midagi muud.

< It started with me wondering if I should bother to tell my mother I was leaving for school.
> See alustas minuga mõtlesin, et lähen ütlema mu ema ära lahkun kooli.

< Not that you can hear me passed out on the kitchen table... Criminy!
> Mitte seda kui sa kuuled mind köögi laua... Krimiini!

< Oh, morning Pheebs...
> Oi, hommikust Pheeb...

< Phoebe's my best friend.
> Phoebe on minu parim sõber

< And a damn good assistant.
> Ja hea pagan abija.

< But of course she's mostly my friend.
> Aga muidugi ta on lihtsalt mu sõber.

< Good morning Helga, how are you today?
> Tere hommikust Helga, kuidas sul läheb täna?

< Oh you know, same ol', same ol'...
> Sa tead küll, sama nii, sama...

< I was lying...
> Ma valetasin

< I was much worse.
> Ma olin palju halvem.

< That's good to hear!
> See on hea kuulda!

< Jeez, feeling perky, Phoebe?
> Oeh, tunned ülemeelik, Phoebe?

< Of course! Since the Cheese Festival is only a few days away now and...
> Muidugi! Alates Juustu Festival on ainult mõned päevad jäänud ja...

< Phoebe's grinning like an idiot, talking about that damn Festival.
> Phoebe narritab nagu idioot, räägib midagi Festival pagan.

< I can't even imagine myself having a good time.
> Ma ei saa uskuda, et saada hea korral.

< So I snap at her...
> Siis ma snäppisin tema...

< I just can't help myself.
> Ma lihtsalt ei saa aitada minu ennast.

< Blah, blah, blah...
> Bla, bla, bla...

< That stupid festival never changes.
> See lollakas festival ei muutu midagi.

< It's the same damn carnival every year.
> See on sama pagan tsirkus igal aastal.

< Big freaking deal...
> Suur paganat soodus...

< I continue to mumble quiet profanities under my breath.
> Ma jätkasin pomisema vaikselt minu hinge.

< Ever since a few years back, whenever they started dating, Phoebe and her boyfriend Gerald were like the "it" couple.
> Isegi alates mõned aastad tagasi, kui nemad hakkasin kohtingu, Phoebe ja tema poisssõber Gerald on nagu armsad.

< He was cool, and she was smart and they just worked out perfectly...I guess...
> Tema poiss on lahe ja tema tüdruk on tark ja see töötas väga hasti...vist...

< I'll never, ever tell her I'm {i}slightly{/i} jealous.
> Ma kunagi mitte, midagi ütlen tema ma olen {i}veidikene{/i} kade.

< Why so down Helga? Don't you find the fair fun anymore?
> Miks sa oled alla, Helga? Kas sa ei leia midagi hea lõbust?

< Phoebe, how can you not remember...
> Phoebe, kuidas sa ei mäleta...

< Then again, why would she? She always ended up not feeling like a miserable failure by the end of it.
> Noh jälle, mis tal on? Ta on alati lõppetanud üles ei tunne nagu ebaõnnestus lõppult.

< Unlike me...
> Mitte nagu mina...

< Never mind, I'm just being negative...or whatever.
> Ei midagi, ma olen lihtsalt negatiivne või mida iganes.

< Negative? Hah. That's a word for it.
> Negatiivne? Ha. See on sõna.

< If you say so.
> Kui sa ütled nii.

< I do say so!
> Ma ütlen nii!

< And while we're on the topic of the Festival...
> Ja kui me oleme teema Festivali...

< Yes?
> Jah?

< There's no way I'm going this year.
> Seal ei ole midagi lähen sel aastal.

< Phoebe frowns deeper...
> Phoebe kortsutab kulmu sügavamalt...

< But why not Helga?
> Aga, miks mitte Helga?

< Even if you've had a bad time before...
> Isegi kui sul on olemas paha aeg enne...

< I cut her off before she can go on.
> Ma lõikan tema välja enne ta saab minna.

< Give it a break Phoebe, criminy...
> Anna mulle puhk, Phoebe... krimiini...

< Why do you even care?
> Miks sa huvitad?

< It's just...
> See on lihtsalt...

< She shakes her head, like she's clearing her thoughts. She seems ready to give me some type of lecture.
> Ta noogutab tema pea nagu ta puhastab oma mõtlemised. Tal on valmis anda mulle midagi tüüpimad loengut.

< It seems to me...
> See tundub mulle...

< Maybe if you tried to focus on something other than...uh...
> Äkki sa proovisid keskuda midagi muud kui...eh...

< ...You-know-who...
> ...Sa tead kes...

< You might be able to enjoy yourself more...
> Sa võid nautida sinu ennast rohkem...

< I nod my head slowly, taking it all in.
> Ma noogutasin pead aeglaselt, võtan kõik sisse.

< Just kidding.
> Tegin nalja.

< I had heard this all before, multiple times in fact.
> Ma kuulsin seda kõik enne, mitut korda faktis.

< Even if I sat her down to explain the insanity of my emotions...
> Isegi kui ma istun tema alla, et seletada minu emotsioonid hullumeelsus...

< She just couldn't understand how hard that was for me, to put him aside.
> Ta lihtsalt ei saa aru kuidas see on raske mulle panna temale.

< She would never understand how most of the time he felt like the only good part in my whole life...
> Ta kunagi ei saa aru kuidas palju kordselt ta tundis nagu hea ainult loogil minu kõik elu...

< The light in my otherwise bleak existence.
> Mu muud sünge olemas on tule.

< But at the very same time, that damn Football Head could ruin me with a smile...
> Aga väga sama kord aeg, see loll Jalgpall Pea võib rikkuda mulle rõõmsaga...

< Especially if that smile was aimed at someone other than me.
> Isegi kui seda rõõmus on paigustatud kellelegi kuid mina.

< And almost always, it was.
> Ja peaaegu alati, see oligi.

< You don't get it.
> Sa ei saa aru.

< What?
> Mida?

< It's not that easy...
> See pole lihtne...

< Helga...
> Helga...

< Ugh, don't pity me Phoebe.
> Ära hakka pihta mind, Phoebe.

< My warning didn't matter, she gives me a pitiful look anyway.
> Minu hoiatus pole tahes, ta annab mulle nägu hale välja.

< I'm used to it now.
> Ma olen kasutanud nüüd.

< I know...
> Ma tean...

< CRASH!!
> PÕMM!!

< Arnold!
> Arnold!

< Helga!
> Helga!

< We've got to stop bumping into each other like this! Haha!
> Me peame lõpetama põmmisemine iga muud nagu seda! Haha!

< Uh...well...
> Noh...jah...

< Got that right, Football Head, one of these days I might actually hurt you!
> Sul on õigus, Jalgpall Pea, üks need päevad ma võiksin haiget teha sulle!

< Whew~
> Oeh~

< Right Helga, whatever you say.
> Hea küll Helga, mida iganes sa ütled.

< Well anyway...
> Noh igatahes...

< He looks around, kind of nervously.
> Ta vaatab ringi, võib olla narviseks.

< Do you mind if I walk with you guys the rest of the way?
> Kas ma võin teile jalutada ülejääl tee?

< I've no issue with that...
> Mul ei ole probleemi sellega...

< Helga?
> Helga?

< Remain calm...calm...calm...
> Võtke rahulikult...rahu...rahu...

< Whatever floats your boat.
> Mida iganes su voolab paati.

< Why is my heart pounding like this?
> Miks mu süda tuksub nagu seda?

< Why does he do this to me?!
> Miks ta tegi mulle seda?!

< Cool, thanks.
> Lahe, äitah.

< So Arnold...
> Kuule Arnold...

< Phoebe's voice breaks through the silence.
> Phoebel hääl lõhkus vaikselt.

< Thank God.
> Jumal tänatud.

< Plan to do anything fun this weekend?
> On teil midagi plaani lõbusat sel puhkusel?

< Oh, wow...
> Oi, vau...

< Phoebe are you asking me to the Cheese Festival?
> Phoebe, kas sa küsid mulle Juustu Festivallisse?

< I really don't think Gerald will be happy about that...
> Ma päriselt ei tea, et Gerald olla rõõmus selle...

< Goodness!
> Taevakene!

< By no means was I implying that...I mean...no!
> Pole tähtus ma mõtlesin seda... ma mõtlen...ei!

< Phoebe looks as if her head is about to explode.
> Phoebe vaatab ehk kui tema pea läheb plahvatama.

< Haha, calm down I'm only teasing...
> Haha, rahu maha ma teen ainult kiusamist...

< To be honest, I don't know if I'm going this year.
> Minu aus ei tea kui ma lähen sel aastal.

< He gives an uneasy shrug of his shoulders.
> Ta annab ei lihtne tema õlad kehitamist.

< They haven't been all that great for me in the past.
> Nemad ei olnud kõik toreaded mulle paari eest.

< I know that feeling...
> Ma tean seda tundus...

< ...!
> ...!

< I didn't mean to say that out loud!
> Ma ei mõelnud öelda kõvasti välja!

< Really Helga?
> Päriselt Helga?

< Why did he have the hear me?
> Miks ta peab kuulama mind?

< Why?
> Miks?

< You haven't had a good time with the Festivals either?
> Sa ei saanud hea aeg koos Festivaalid?

< I didn't say that...
> Ma ei ütlenud seda...

< No, you did, you just said...
> Ei, sa tegid, sa lihtsalt ütlesid...

< It doesn't matter what I said, hey look!
> See pole tahes mis ma ütlesin, oi vaata!

< I point out the looming, big, brown building.
> Ma näitasin hägeva, suur, pruun ehitus.

< It's the school!
> See on kool!

< Anyway the festival...
> Igatahes festival...

< Phoebe tries to pull his attention away from me...
> Phoebe proovib tõsta tema tähelepanelikult eemale minust...

< I suppose my showing him where the school was...wasn't good enough.
> Ma lihtsalt minu nähtus koos tema kus on kool oli...ei olnud hästi aitamist.

< It's on Saturday. Can you believe it?
> See on laupäev. Saaksid uskuda?

< Wow, only three more days?
> Vau, ainult kolm päeva veel?

< Whoopee~
> Uupsiii~

< That they decide to ignore.
> Siis, nemad otsustasid ignoneerida.

< Suddenly Arnold turns towards the school.
> Arnold pöörab enda kooli poole.

< Ugh...
> Ah...

< I gotta rush...my class is all the way on the other side of the building.
> Ma pean jooksma...mu klassiruum on igal poolesse teise poole ehitusel.

< Well, I'll see you guys later!
> Noh, ma näen teile hiljem!

< There walks the love of my life...
> Seal jalutab armastus minu elust...

< Completely oblivious as always.
> Täitsa unustlik alati.

< As we get closer to the entrance of the school, I notice I start to slow down...
> Me saame lähedaselt kooli sisseminekut, ma teatsin hakkasin aeglaselt minema...

< I really don't wanna be here right now...
> Ma päriselt ei taha olla seal kohe...

< I stop completely, finding a stone on the sidewalk more interesting then moving on.
> Ma peatusin lõplikult, leian kivi pool jalutuse on veel huvitava ja siis liigun edasi.

< Phoebe, I think I'm just gonna skip class...
> Phoebe, äkki ma lihtsalt jätan klassi vahele...

< Helga that's not wise...
> Helga, see pole hea mõte...

< I know but...
> Ma tean, aga...

< I promise I'll be back before the afternoon classes start...
> Ma luban tulen tagasi enne pärast lõunat klassis alustab...

< I just gotta...
> Ma pidin...

< I want to give her a valid excuse, something better than...than...
> Ma tahtsin anda temale kehtiv vabandus, midagi parem kui...kui...

< Think or something...
> Mõtleda või midagi...

< Better than that.
> Parem kuni seda.

< Well, okay. I'll take notes for you.
> Noh, hea küll. Ma võtan märkmikud sulle.

< Thanks...
> Äitah...

< It's all I could think to say.
> See ongi kõik öelda mõtlemisel.

< Bye-bye.
> Head aega.

< I turn and leave without a word and, somehow, after a long while of aimlessly walking...
> Ma pöörasin ja lahkusin ilma sõnata ja kuidagi pärast kaua jalutuse käikul...

< I end up at the festival grounds.
> Ma lõpetasin üles festival alus.

< The whole place looks like some type of horror movie in the making.
> Terve koht oleks nagu mõned tüüpi hirmus filmi tegemist.

< It was completely abandoned...I guess the guys who were suppose to set it up were on break.
> See on täitsa vanasti... ma arvan need mehed tulid installima olid vaheajal.

< I took a look around anyway...
> Ma võtsin ja vaatsin igalpool...

< The only thing this place brought up in me was bad memories.
> Ainult tingimus on see koht tuli üles minul oli paha mälestused.

< It was like I could see every unsuccessful scheme flash before my eyes.
> See oleks nagu näinudki kõik iga ebaõnnestus välku enne mu silmad.

< Ugh, my plans never go right!
> Ah, mu plaanid ei lähe hästi!

< I felt like the best thing to do at this point was to fall down, maybe curl up and sleep.
> Ma tundsin nagu parim tingimus on teha sel point oli kukuda maha, äkki ülesse ja magada.

< Was there even a point to evil plans and plots anymore?
> Kas oli seal point kurja plaanid ja joonis midagi?

< Even if I ruined Arnold's time, he always ended up kind of, sort of happy in the end.
> Isegi kui ma rikkun Arnoldi aega, ta alati lõpetab üles, olla rõõmus lõppus.

< That beautiful, damn-it-all, always looking on the bright side attitude.
> See ilus, pagan kõik, alati vaatan ilusat poole asend.

< And that's when it hit me...I should get to him before he even has a chance to ask someone else.
> Ja see kui lõi mind... ma võtan temasse enne kui tal on valik küsida kellegi käest.

< I should just get him to bring me!
> Ma vist võtan tema, et tuua mind!

< That's it!
> Täpselt nii!

< The real question though, was how...
> Päris küsimus oli kuidas...

< It's obvious that by now, after all these years, Arnold isn't exactly used to a nice, ask-this-girl-out-right-now, type of personality from me...
> See on ilmne kohe seda, pärast kõik aastad, Arnold ei olnud kasutanud kenaks, küsida tüdruku välja kohe, tüüpi isiku minust...

< But I could try, couldn't I? To be just a little nicer to him, a little kinder...
> Aga ma võin proovida, kas võiksin? Lihtsalt olla väike kena tema, natuke kenam...

< It wasn't that much of a stretch.
> See ei olnud palju venitus.

< Could he be swayed?
> Kas ta saab kõikunud?

< Could I...his one true love...finally win his heart?!
> Kas ma...tema üks päris armas...lõpuks võitab tema süda?!

< This would have to be handled delicately, any wrong choice could completely botch things up.
> See oleks saada korras pidada, iga valesti valikud võib tekkida lõplikult lõhkuda üles.

< Without another thought I turn around and head back towards the school...
> Ilma teise arvamus ma pööran tagasi kooli juurdesse...

< This time I was going to be successful! I was sure of it...
> See kord ma läheksin saada õnnestus! Ma olen kindel...

< Helga G. Pataki, Saturday night is gonna be your night ol' girl!
> Helga G. Pataki, laupäev öö on sinu öö tüdruk!

< I somehow make it back just in time for lunch and catch Arnold standing on line for food...
> Mõnes korras sain tagasi ajal lõunal ja püüda Arnold seisab järjelkorjas toidust...

< Lunch came quicker than I expected it too...
> Lõunasöögiks tuli kiirem kuna ma mõtlesin ka...

< And I catch Arnold on the food line.
> Ja ma püüan Arnold toidu järjel.

< Without really thinking on it...
> Ilma väga päris mõtlemine...

< I casually cut the person standing behind him and take his spot.
> Ma sadun tulla inimese eest ära olla taga ja võta tema koht.

< But what do I do?...
> Aga mida ma teen?...

< Hey Arnoldo, how's it hanging?
> Tere Arnoldo, kuidas läheb?

< Oh, hey Helga...
> Oi, tere Helga...

< I didn't see you in class...
> Ma ei ole näinud sind klassis...

< Nope, I skipped.
> Ei, jätsin vahele.

< Oh yeah? Any reason?
> Oojah? On midagi põhjust?

< I just needed some time to think is all...
> Mul oli just aega võtta midagi mõtleda välja kõik...

< That excuse seems to be working for me today.
> Selle vabadamise võiks töötada mulle täna.

< Nothing to worry your handsome Football Head about...
> Pole midagi muretsema su kallis Jalgpall Pea sellest...

< Did I really say that out loud and the world didn't explode?
> Kas ma päriselt ütlesin kõva hääle ja maailma pole plahvatanud?

< .......
> .......

< Why isn't he saying anything!?
> Miks ta ei ütle midagi!?

< Well that's good, you were missed.
> Noh see on hea, sa jätsid vahele.

< He must think that I'm trying to tease him.
> Ta mõtleb seda, et ma proovin narrida temale.

< I'm not sure if that's a good thing or a bad thing.
> Ma pole kindel, et kas on hea tingimus või häbi tingimus.

< Oh was I now? Did you miss me Arnold?
> Oi, kas olin kohe? Kas igatsesid mind, Arnold?

< Yeah, I missed you kicking the back of my chair, Helga...
> Jah, igatsesin sind lööda tagant minu tooli, Helga...

< I've learned I can't live without it...
> Ma olen õppinud, et ei saa elada ilma...

< Is this flirting...or is he making fun of me?
> Kas see huvi...või ta teeb nalja mind?

< Or is it both.......?
> Või see on mõlemad..?

< Good to know, I'll kick it extra hard tomorrow.
> Hea mõtleda, ma proovin lööda lisa rasket homseks.

< Just for you!
> Lihtsalt sulle!

< Heh. I can do it too!
> Hah. Ma saan ka teha!

< Great, hah, it's a date.
> Tore, hah, see on kohtumine.

< How's your day so far?
> Kuidas su kaugel päev?

< You ask me like you weren't there for some of it...
> Sa küsid mind nagu sa ei ole seal mõnes...

< Haha, yeah, that's true.
> Haha, jah, see on õige.

< I'm gonna take a wild guess here and say, "boring"?
> Ma võtan selle asja siit ja ütlen, "igav"?

< Ding-ding-ding...you win a prize.
> Ding-ding-ding...sa võitsid auhinna.

< My voice is rather sarcastic...but he keeps smiling at me.
